    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d854">

                <pb facs="0786" n="614" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg614"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 703.5262/19</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé d’Affaires in the Netherlands</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Langhorne</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">The Hague</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-30T16:00:00+01:19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 30, 1917, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 1, 2 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1026. Spanish Minister informs me that German Government will withdraw permission
                    for Americans to work at Spanish Embassy, Berlin, if German employees at Swiss
                    Legation, Washington, are dismissed, and expresses hope that this situation may
                    not arise as the departure of the few Americans now at the Embassy would impair
                    efficiency of its work.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Langhorne</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
